  "id": "DrugBank_DB11576 - MONDO_1239",
  "verbalization": "Ferric oxide is associated with anemia of prematurity through a mechanistic pathway involving ferrous gluconate. The evidence suggests that ferric oxide may be used to treat deficiency anemia, hypochromic anemia, and iron deficiency anemia, all of which are linked to anemia of prematurity. The indication chain indicates that ferric oxide may be used as a therapeutic agent to address the underlying iron deficiency that contributes to this condition. The final scores from the paths suggest a strong, though not absolute, correlation between ferric oxide and anemia of prematurity, likely due to its role in correcting iron deficiency. The mechanism of action is inferred through the indirect pathway involving ferrous gluconate, which is a known treatment for anemia of prematurity. The evidence supports a plausible mechanistic link, but further validation through clinical trials or more direct experimental evidence would be necessary to confirm the therapeutic efficacy of ferric oxide in this context.",
